# SPAMS ESP32 — Copy-Pasteable Arduino Codes

Each sketch below is complete. Copy each code block into a **separate Arduino IDE sketch** of the matching name.

**Note:** These are prototype scripts. Set gateway Wi-Fi and the private device token, and keep the node UUIDs matched to the Supabase registry. The API accepts pH, TDS, turbidity voltage, and raw water-level ADC after applying the water-quality migration. pH and turbidity in NTU remain unavailable until calibrated; raw level counts are not meters.

## SPAMS_Central_Gateway.ino
# DEVICE_TOKEN=03475a73ac20677c158e2562adc7c46c528e269ea09569d73fcda015159207df
# TOKEN_HASH=ff00a368cc19cd1c900bdbd505c918f3540fbfafcd6fa77e774d7be8dd6cc1e0
```cpp
/* SPAMS: two-node ESP-NOW -> authenticated HTTPS gateway.
 * Target: original ESP32 DevKit/WROOM; Arduino-ESP32 core 3.x.
 * Demo only: no pump, no solar/battery measurement, no acoustic classifier.
 * IMPORTANT: provision hardware gateway + two node UUIDs in Supabase first.
 */
#include <WiFi.h>
#include <esp_now.h>
#include <esp_wifi.h>
#include <esp_system.h>
#include <HTTPClient.h>
#include <WiFiClientSecure.h>
#include <time.h>
#include <freertos/FreeRTOS.h>
#include <freertos/queue.h>

// EDIT THESE VALUES. Do not put the device credential in GitHub.
